# False positives: node/npm CVEs reported against python:3.14-slim base image
# mein-assistent has no Node.js runtime (no package.json, no npm, no node on PATH)
# Trivy picks these up from the GitHub Actions runner, not the container image.
# Verified false positive: HBE-1657 (2026-07-02)
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802
# CVE-2024-21538: cross-spawn (npm) ReDoS
# False positive: python:3.14-slim has no Node.js/npm runtime; no package.json in image
# Trivy attributing npm CVE from GitHub Actions runner environment
# Accepted: 2026-07-04, Owner: Jonas (Engineering), Ref: HBE-1768
CVE-2024-21538
# CVE-2026-59873/59874: tar (npm) DoS via gzip bomb / malformed tar header
# False positive: same runner-attribution pattern as above — mein-assistent has no Node.js
# runtime and no npm packages in the container image; tar npm package not present.
# Accepted: 2026-07-22, Owner: Jonas (Engineering), Ref: HBE-2400
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874
# CVE-2026-13149: brace-expansion (npm) DoS via exponential-time O(2^n) expansion
# False positive: same runner-attribution pattern — mein-assistent is a pure Python/Streamlit app
# with no Node.js runtime, no npm, no package.json in the container image. Trivy picks up
# brace-expansion from the GitHub Actions runner environment, not from the container image.
# Accepted: 2026-07-22, Owner: Jonas (Engineering), Ref: HBE-2404
CVE-2026-13149

